<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; connect-src 'none'; img-src 'none'; font-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; worker-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'">
  <title>S147 — Client-side correctness oracle</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="lesson.css">
  <script src="fixtures.js" defer></script>
  <script src="model.js" defer></script>
  <script src="app.js" defer></script>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <p class="banner">Training rehearsal - synthetic data - not a live Azure result</p>
    <h1>S147 — Client-side correctness oracle</h1>
    <p>A-S147 · original S · P0 · SC-S147 · SOURCE</p>
    <p>Inspect misleading 200/state-loss/duplicate fixtures; choose the correct client-side failure verdicts.</p>
    <p class="warning">HTTP 200, readiness and throughput do not prove preserved user state or exactly-one effect.</p>
  </header>
  <main>
    <section aria-labelledby="contract-heading">
      <h2 id="contract-heading">Before the rehearsal</h2>
      <p>Preconditions: a standard JavaScript-enabled browser and these local files. Every client, request, response, identity, version, state, effect, outcome and metric is fixed fictional teaching DATA ONLY.</p>
      <p>No API, network request, account, user data, business operation, storage, cloud, credentials, deployment or spending is used. The operator console itself is not the fictional broken UI.</p>
      <p>Source: README S147 requires detection of empty success, silent logout, lost state, duplicate effects and broken UI, not just HTTP status. D-S147 requires every injected acceptance failure to be flagged without relying solely on HTTP/health status.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="exercise-heading">
      <h2 id="exercise-heading">Conduct → inspect → select → check</h2>
      <p>Select one of eight fixed fixtures. Complete a check before starting another run. Each run permits three checks; all eight runs remain until explicit reset, with no eviction.</p>
      <form id="exercise-form" novalidate>
        <label for="fixture-picker">Fixed fictional fixture</label>
        <select id="fixture-picker" name="fixture">
          <option value="">Choose a fixture</option>
        </select>
        <button id="conduct-button" type="button">1. Conduct fixture</button>
        <button id="inspect-button" type="button" disabled>2. Inspect client evidence</button>
        <label for="verdict-picker">Your client-side verdict</label>
        <select id="verdict-picker" name="verdict" disabled>
          <option value="">Choose a verdict</option>
          <option value="CLIENT-SIDE FAILURE">CLIENT-SIDE FAILURE</option>
          <option value="CLIENT-SIDE CORRECT">CLIENT-SIDE CORRECT</option>
          <option value="UNKNOWN">UNKNOWN</option>
        </select>
        <button id="check-button" type="submit" disabled>3. Check selection</button>
      </form>
      <p id="error-output" role="alert" tabindex="-1" hidden></p>
      <p id="status-output" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready. No fictional journey has been conducted.</p>
      <button id="lesson-reset" type="button">Reset fictional rehearsal and clear its history</button>
      <noscript>This lesson needs JavaScript. No results can be inferred when it is unavailable.</noscript>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="trace-heading">
      <h2 id="trace-heading">Fixed trace — inspect facts, not health alone</h2>
      <p id="fixture-description">No fixture selected.</p>
      <pre id="trace-output" tabindex="0" aria-label="Fixed fictional request and observation trace">No trace yet.</pre>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="assertions-heading">
      <h2 id="assertions-heading">Client assertions</h2>
      <p>Exactly five assertions per observed or unobserved attempt: nonempty response, authentication/identity/session, preserved state/version, exactly-one keyed effect, usable compatible UI. Missing required observations are UNKNOWN.</p>
      <p id="assertion-summary">No assertions inspected.</p>
      <pre id="assertions-output" tabindex="0" aria-label="Exact client assertion JSON">[]</pre>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="impact-heading">
      <h2 id="impact-heading">Original user impact — never rewritten by recovery</h2>
      <p>The denominator is original journeys, not requests, checks, retries or later recovery attempts. An originally interrupted journey stays interrupted; an original missing observation stays unknown. Later recovery is a separate, overlapping count.</p>
      <p id="impact-summary">No original impact inspected.</p>
      <pre id="impact-output" tabindex="0" aria-label="Exact original user impact JSON">null</pre>
      <pre id="journeys-output" tabindex="0" aria-label="Original journeys and separate later attempts JSON">null</pre>
      <h3>Independent fictional transport signals</h3>
      <p>Transport denominators count attempt records, not completed original journeys. The reported 240 requests/second is a fixed fictional signal, not a measured benchmark.</p>
      <pre id="transport-output" tabindex="0" aria-label="Fictional transport JSON">null</pre>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="check-heading">
      <h2 id="check-heading">Detection, expected-negative conformance and learner check</h2>
      <p>A detected client failure, an expected-negative conformance PASS and a correct learner PASS are separate facts. None changes an interrupted or unknown original journey into success.</p>
      <pre id="conformance-output" tabindex="0" aria-label="Expected-negative conformance JSON">null</pre>
      <pre id="check-output" tabindex="0" aria-label="Learner verifier JSON">No selection checked.</pre>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="history-heading">
      <h2 id="history-heading">Retained rehearsal history</h2>
      <p>Replaying the same fixed fixture is another exercise, not a new user measurement. Impact is reported per fixture, never summed across repeated runs.</p>
      <p id="history-summary">0 / 8 retained runs.</p>
      <ol id="history-output"></ol>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="limits-heading">
      <h2 id="limits-heading">Limits and blocked native remainder</h2>
      <p>This bounded exercise flags the five supplied observed failures only. It cannot certify every real failure, health endpoint, browser, migration, UI, identity provider, data store, exactly-once system or reliability target.</p>
      <p>B-S147 remains blocked on CORE, DATA and HOST, native isolated fault injection and independent client-side oracle evidence. The original source-demo acceptance is not complete. This original A unit can earn at most one S credit after the parent’s empirical acceptance; tests, repairs and refinement earn zero extra credits.</p>
      <p>Local browser evidence uses approved offline Playwright 1.56.1, Microsoft-signed Edge 156 and Node 22. It is not Node 24 production or native Azure proof. The inactive browser lifecycle prototype is unqualified; only the published isolated helper is used.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
